---
description: Enforced spec-driven development team rules (always apply)
alwaysApply: true
---

The canonical team rules live in AGENTS.md at the repo root - read and follow
them in every session. Summary: all source changes go through the spec-kit
workflow (`/speckit-specify` → `/speckit-plan` → `/speckit-tasks` →
`/speckit-implement`); uncovered changes are regularized with
`/speckit-backfill` and verified with `/speckit-comply`; hooks deny source
writes outside the workflow - when denied, run the command the denial message
names instead of working around it. Never set SPECKIT_ENFORCE=0 or use
`git commit --no-verify` unless a human explicitly instructs it.

Foundational standards first: a new project MUST run `/speckit-start` to
establish its standards (Constitution, Frameworks, Security, and Design if it
has a UI) before any source work; the pre-write hook blocks source writes until
the required standards exist. Change a standard via `/speckit-update-standards`.
At session start, read these if present and treat them as binding:
`.specify/memory/constitution.md`, `frameworks.md`, `security.md`, `design.md`
(UI only), and the `standards.json` manifest. See `docs/STANDARDS.md`.
